## NuGet
*.nupkg
*.snupkg

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials. Nothing below this line may ever be committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Local Vault snapshots. A pulled tier is a plaintext copy of every secret in
# it - bank keys, database passwords, signing material.
snapshots/

# Backups written before a promote. Same content, same reason.
*.bak.*

# .NET user secrets, if one is ever placed in the tree rather than in the
# per-user store where VaultSettingsStore puts it.
secrets.json

# Environment files and key material.
.env
*.env
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
*.key

# Per-developer Vault connection settings: addresses, namespaces and secret
# paths for whatever this working copy happens to point at. Tokens never reach
# it (VaultConnection.Token is [JsonIgnore]), but the rest still describes a
# real deployment. Ship appsettings.example.json instead.
JsonInsight/appsettings.json
WebJsonInsight/appsettings.json

## Editors / OS
*.user
*.suo
~$*
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local reference payloads copied from a real deployment (sample nodes, pasted
# responses). Same reasoning as appsettings.json above: they name real hosts,
# so they stay out of the repository — and out of the hygiene scan with it.
docs/sample jsons/
